{"type":"message","id":"d12feecd","parentId":"6a4969d2","timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:05:41.238Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Accidental 35.2% → \"35% excess\" matches with simple definition. Good.\n\nOlder vs younger: the raw effect not monotonic but 80s has 12%, 90s 8.8%, 70s -2.9%. Hmm. Maybe the story uses seasonally-adjusted expected (the proper method) rather than simple count/(N/365). Or they compare age groups with z-scores. Need find the story chart/definitions. Maybe there's a chart with age groups and values. Text: \"Unlike Peña... I actually found that the birthday effect was stronger in older versus younger people.\" Could be a chart labeled \"Birthday effect by age\" with values. We need view chart labels. web_view didn't show them—maybe charts are SVG with text that the browser tool didn't capture because animation? Could try scrolling slower? web_view automatically scrolls. The page text output omitted chart labels entirely, strange. Maybe charts are canvas drawn via JS; no text. We can try web_fetch on page with different user agent? Not.\n\nMaybe story has a methods/data notes link. Main text \"Data and methods\" section is inline, no link. There may be links to studies only.\n\nCould inspect the HTML via web_fetch? It returns parsed text, not scripts. Maybe use r.jina.ai? web_fetch to https://r.jina.ai/https://pudding.cool/... might return full text/markdown, perhaps chart labels? But external service. Could try. Or Google cache. Let's try web_fetch on r.jina.ai URL.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_eLbjTw1VXEBo1ImvgSJY0907","name":"web_fetch","arguments":{"url":"https://r.jina.ai/https://pudding.cool/2025/04/birthday-effect/"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_OZiirnfZ3JwEnJv9dQkN2206","name":"web_fetch","arguments":{"url":"https://pudding.cool/2025/04/birthday-effect/index.html"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-flash","usage":{